id: pm-ap7ilf
title: MCP create drops advertised metadata outside its small top-level allowlist
description: "Independent stateless stdio reproduction while addressing pm-gh1538: pm_create advertises deadline but ignores a top-level deadline=2026-11-01 with title/type and options.createMode=progressive, returns success and creates an item with no deadline. The same shared SDK hoist path also omits explicit create id and other canonical metadata. Extend canonical parameter normalization and atomic malformed-value preflight to create while preserving native SDK input admission, custom fields, nested aliases and template/type resolution."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T23:10:30.182Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T01:06:55.545Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-22T01:06:54.046Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T01:06:54.046Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Persist schema-advertised create metadata including explicit id and deadline; Explicit nested values and equivalent aliases retain precedence; Malformed typed fields refuse before creating any item or history; Public MCP and SDK compatibility plus packed npm and Bun consumers pass
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: medium
confidence: 95
severity: medium
resolution: "Create consumes the shared canonical mutation source including id, deadline, completion metadata, repeatables and booleanish false values; nested aliases and custom workspace metadata remain supported."
expected_result: Create persists declared metadata and rejects malformed values before item/history writes while preserving project customization and nested alias precedence.
actual_result: "Create retains requested id, deadline, estimate, linked files, custom delivery_channel and regression=false; imported terminal work retains its supplied ISO completed_at and verified history. Nested id/estimatedMinutes and false allow_missing_parent controls pass. Malformed create requests leave task/history snapshots byte-identical; packed npm/Bun consumers and full coverage pass."
