comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T23:10:30.182Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh request-specific search, open/in-progress inventories and the complete all-status corpus found closed numeric-priority and metadata-surface work but no owner for advertised top-level create values being dropped. This is distinct from the active update-only report. Confirmed through the current built public stdio entrypoint in an isolated non-git tracker with production telemetry disabled. Bundle this matching SDK normalization fix with pm-gh1538 and pm-gh1539 in one reviewed delivery."
  "2026-10-21T23:22:07.163Z","harness:codex","Implementation and focused evidence: modern MCP create now persists explicit id, deadline, estimate and a declared custom delivery_channel field; nested id and estimatedMinutes beat flat aliases. Malformed priority/type/list/container values refuse with changed=false and all task/history bytes unchanged. A nested false allow_missing_parent also wins over flat true. Strict MCP warning reporting exposed false warnings for valid runtime aliases and declared custom fields; shared SDK alias contracts and the public field lookup now prevent those false diagnostics without allowlisting them. The20 focused mutation/native-admission/MCP compatibility tests pass."
  "2026-10-21T23:46:52.065Z","harness:codex","A final contract census compared every advertised create/update parameter with the SDK normalization sources. Update has no unmapped mutation parameters; create still declares closeReason and completedAt as ad hoc extras outside TOOL_CREATE_OPTION_CONTRACT_SOURCE. Their CLI registration and domain options already exist. Add them to the canonical option source, remove the duplicate schema extras, and prove persisted imported-terminal metadata before final packing. This avoids leaving two advertised fields on the old no-op path."
  "2026-10-22T00:00:36.053Z","harness:codex","The imported-terminal control failed before the canonical tuple correction: the supplied completedAt was replaced by the current creation time. Adding closeReason/completedAt to the shared source makes the same isolated test preserve the requested ISO completion time and verify history. The supported regression=false case also exposed a lossy scalar conversion; explicit false now uses the declared booleanish metadata contract while true retains flag-presence semantics. The main fixture covers both plus harmless false controls."
  "2026-10-22T00:43:49.045Z","harness:codex","Full-suite follow-up: 10980 tests passed and two existing fixed-count assertions still expected43 canonical create parameters. Correct their explicit census to45 for the added completion fields, preserving independent literal counts and the full parity checks. This changes no production code or gate threshold. Rerun both focused census suites before the complete coverage run."
  "2026-10-22T01:06:52.715Z","harness:codex","Final verification: the packed public SDK passes strict TypeScript 5.9.3 declarations, deliberately degraded literal/exactness control, restored declarations, and Node/Bun activation and runtime identity. Maintained packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx smoke passes. All linked tests pass and the complete repository coverage run passes with 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. No coverage denominator, timeout, assertion or quality threshold was reduced. Source-level static checks, import costs and transport floors passed; the graph gate identified new prose references and was repaired through explicit related edges instead of a limit change. The final full static pipeline, terminal defect evidence and generated changelog are required before push."
